      "writtenOn": "2024-07-25T23:33:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you explain a bit more? If I run my raw os images directly on crosvm with these args, I get both output and input working:\n\n```\nadb shell \"/apex/com.android.virt/bin/crosvm --extended-status run --disable-sandbox --mem 256 --host-cpu-topology --virt-cpufreq --serial type\u003dstdout,stdin,hardware\u003dvirtio-console,num\u003d1 --initrd \u003cinitrd\u003e \u003ckernel\u003e\n```\n\nBut when using AVF only output works. The main difference is that AVF is type\u003dfile for the serial configuration:\n```\n--serial\u003dtype\u003dfile,path\u003d/proc/self/fd/29 (/dev/ptmx),input\u003d/proc/self/fd/30 (/dev/pts/0),hardware\u003dvirtio-console,num\u003d1\n```\n\nwhich leads me to believe that something on the host-side is not properly configuring the pipes.",
